 "final_summary": "The test failed because the priority validation logic incorrectly treated the upper bound as exclusive (using `priority >= PRIORITY_MAX`). The fix changed the condition to `priority > PRIORITY_MAX`, making the upper bound inclusive. This allows priority 5 to be accepted, matching the expected behavior.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/validation.py b/tracker/validation.py\nindex 0c3a585..df7a817 100644\n--- a/tracker/validation.py\n+++ b/tracker/validation.py\n@@ -45,10 +45,9 @@ def _clean_priority(value):\n     priority = parse_int(value, name=\"priority\")\n     if priority is None:\n         raise ValidationError(\"priority must not be null\", {\"priority\": \"required\"})\n-    if priority < PRIORITY_MIN or priority >= PRIORITY_MAX:\n-        raise ValidationError(\n-            f\"priority must be between {PRIORITY_MIN} and {PRIORITY_MAX}\", {\"priority\": \"out_of_range\"}\n-        )\n+    if priority < PRIORITY_MIN or priority > PRIORITY_MAX:\n+        raise ValidationError(f\"priority must be between {PRIORITY_MIN} and {PRIORITY_MAX}\", {\"priority\": \"out_of_range\"})\n+    return priority\n     return priority\n \n \n",
